---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ServiceCards from '../../components/ServiceCards.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Energy & Building Compliance Services Scotland" description="Commercial EPCs, Section 63, SAP, SBEM, DSM, TM59, DECs and fire risk assessments from Glasgow, with service coverage across Scotland and the UK.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" data-reveal>
      <h1 class="section-title">Technical services portfolio</h1>
      <p class="lead">Our nine-service structure supports transactions, development programmes, statutory obligations, and ongoing portfolio compliance across the UK.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <ServiceCards />
  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <h2>Choose the right assessment for the project</h2>
    <p>For a commercial sale or new letting, start with <a href="/services/commercial-epcs">the EPC requirements</a> and check whether <a href="/services/section-63-assessments">Section 63</a> also applies. A <a href="/services/decs">DEC</a> serves a different operational-rating purpose.</p>
    <p>For development work, <a href="/services/saps">SAP</a> addresses dwellings and <a href="/services/sbem-calculations">SBEM</a> addresses non-domestic assessment. Scottish projects use the applicable Building Standards and Section 6 guidance; Part L references concern other UK jurisdictions. <a href="/services/dynamic-simulation-modelling-dsm">Dynamic simulation</a> and <a href="/services/overheating-assessments-tm59">TM59</a> support more detailed performance questions.</p>
  </div></section>
  <CTASection title="Need help selecting the right scope?" text="Tell us where your project is now and what you need to evidence. We will advise the most efficient service path." />
</BaseLayout>
